schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: A private key exclusively controls signing authority over a blockchain account
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    "Your private key has the power to control your entire account. This
    allows you to make decisions on the blockchain, or in other words, sign
    transactions."
  evidence: >-
    Direct quotation attributed to "[Source S]" in how-transactions-work.md's
    "Signing" step, which the article's References section identifies as
    Ledger Academy: How Does a Blockchain Transaction Work.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/how-transactions-work.md
  interpretation: >-
    Used to explain why a private key must never be shared — it is the sole
    mechanism proving transaction authorization.
  uncertainty: >-
    Quote reproduced as given in the article; exact wording was not
    independently checked against the live Ledger Academy page for this
    ingestion.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/how-transactions-work.md
    transformation: quoted
    authorship: ai-assisted
